\section{Collider Phenomenology}

In this section we analyze the collider phenomenology of the STME-RS-A framework.
The anharmonic KK spectrum produces distinct multi-TeV resonances in di-lepton,
di-photon, and di-jet channels. We compute production cross sections, resonance
shapes, detector resolution effects, and HL-LHC sensitivity for benchmark points
BP1--BP4.

\subsection{Production Channels}

KK modes couple to quarks, gluons, and electroweak gauge bosons. The dominant
production mechanisms at the HL-LHC are:
\begin{itemize}
\item quark-antiquark annihilation: $q\bar{q} \to \phi_n$,
\item gluon fusion: $gg \to \phi_n$,
\item vector boson fusion: $VV \to \phi_n$.
\end{itemize}

The partonic cross section is
\begin{equation}
\hat{\sigma}(ij \to \phi_n) =
\frac{\pi}{12} \frac{g_{n,i}^2}{m_n^2}
\delta(\hat{s} - m_n^2),
\end{equation}
where $g_{n,i}$ is the coupling of the KK mode to partons $i,j$.

The hadronic cross section is
\begin{equation}
\sigma(pp \to \phi_n) =
\sum_{i,j}
\int dx_1 dx_2\, f_i(x_1) f_j(x_2)
\hat{\sigma}(ij \to \phi_n).
\end{equation}

