\end{figure}

\subsection{Resonance Shapes}

The KK modes appear as narrow resonances in invariant mass distributions. The
Breit--Wigner line shape is
\begin{equation}
\frac{d\sigma}{dm} \propto
\frac{m_n \Gamma_n}{(m^2 - m_n^2)^2 + m_n^2 \Gamma_n^2},
\end{equation}
where $\Gamma_n$ is the total decay width.

Anharmonicity modifies both $m_n$ and $\Gamma_n$, producing distinct resonance
patterns.

