\subsection{Detector Resolution Effects}

Detector resolution smears the resonance peaks. The observed distribution is
\begin{equation}
\frac{d\sigma_{\text{obs}}}{dm} =
\int dm'\, G(m - m'; \sigma_{\text{det}})
\frac{d\sigma}{dm'},
\end{equation}
where $G$ is a Gaussian with width $\sigma_{\text{det}}$.

For multi-TeV resonances, typical resolution values are:
\begin{align}
\sigma_{\text{det}}^{\ell\ell} &\approx 1.5\%, \\
\sigma_{\text{det}}^{\gamma\gamma} &\approx 2.0\%, \\
\sigma_{\text{det}}^{jj} &\approx 8.0\%.
\end{align}

