\caption{Detector resolution effects for di-lepton, di-photon, and di-jet
channels. Di-jet resolution significantly broadens KK resonances.}
\label{fig:detector_resolution}
\end{figure}

\subsection{HL-LHC Sensitivity}

We compute the HL-LHC sensitivity for BP1--BP4 using
$\sqrt{s}=13.6~\text{TeV}$ and $3~\text{ab}^{-1}$ of integrated luminosity.

The significance is
\begin{equation}
Z = \sqrt{2\left[(S+B)\ln\left(1+\frac{S}{B}\right) - S\right]},
\end{equation}
where $S$ and $B$ are signal and background yields.

For BP1--BP4, the first three KK modes yield:
\begin{align}
Z_1 &\in [4.1, 7.8], \\
Z_2 &\in [3.5, 6.2], \\
Z_3 &\in [2.1, 4.9].
\end{align}

